            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0432" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/1097</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-19">July 19, 1930</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I attach hereto, for the Department’s confidential files, (until the texts are
                    made public by the Guatemalan and Honduran Governments) the carbon copies of the
                    texts of the Arbitration Treaty and Supplementary Convention, signed by the
                    representatives of Guatemala and Honduras on the afternoon of July 16, 1930.
                    These carbons are the exact copies of the Guatemalan and Honduran copies as
                    signed. I also attach copies of the English translations of this Treaty and
                    Convention, as agreed upon by the Guatemalan and Honduran Delegations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis White</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d328-a1.xml" xpointer="d328-a1"/>
